WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
- We're here with one of my
favorite actors, Adam Scott.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.227
And he's also a film buff who stars in

00:00:06.227 --> 00:00:09.381
the new Apple TV+ show "Severance".

00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:11.790
(audience applause)

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.840
So we're gonna test your
knowledge of best pictures

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.071
from Oscars winners of the past.

00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:21.219
And if Adam can guess four correct,

00:00:21.219 --> 00:00:23.790
we're throwing an Oscar's pizza party

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.770
for everyone in our audience.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.603
That's right.

00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:31.510
Everyone's gonna get a
gift card for not one,

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.420
not two, not three, not
four, not five, but six

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.934
deep dish pizzas from Chicago's very own

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:42.380
the wonderful Lou Malnati's,
which is like famous.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.913
So famous.
- Delicious.

00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:46.011
So...

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:47.260
- So pressure's on...

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.072
If I don't get them right, then we...

00:00:50.072 --> 00:00:51.750
They don't get a pizza party.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.100
Is that what's happening?

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.600
- I don't know, Adam, the
pizzas are in your hands.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.433
Are you ready?

00:00:56.433 --> 00:00:57.700
- Okay.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.533
Yes, I am.

00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:02.420
- Okay, first up it's
a movie from the 1970s.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.601
See if you know what it is.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:06.950
- Oh, Godfather.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:07.783
- Yeah.
(ding)

00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.557
Yeah, a hundred percent.

00:01:09.557 --> 00:01:11.339
A hundred percent!

00:01:11.339 --> 00:01:13.170
Ding, ding, ding, ding.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.290
All right, we're going to the eighties

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.470
and the next poster piece is...

00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:20.319
- "Chariots of Fire".

00:01:20.319 --> 00:01:21.680
- Ding ding ding ding!

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.847
Yes, yes, yes!

00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:25.523
Show me the nineties!

00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:30.447
- "Forrest Gump".

00:01:30.447 --> 00:01:31.672
- Yes!

00:01:31.672 --> 00:01:34.186
(Drew cheering)
(audience applause)

00:01:34.186 --> 00:01:35.870
- All right, I can taste the pizza.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.510
I can smell the pizza.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.800
It's getting close.
- I can smell it!

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.280
- I see cheese oozing.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.113
Okay.

00:01:42.113 --> 00:01:44.013
Moving on to this century.

00:01:46.142 --> 00:01:48.259
- Oh, "Slumdog Millionaire".

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:49.590
- Yes!

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.590
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:01:52.949 --> 00:01:53.933
Guess what!

00:01:53.933 --> 00:01:54.860
- [Adam] Is that it?

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:55.756
- You did it!

00:01:55.756 --> 00:01:56.889
That's four right.

00:01:56.889 --> 00:01:59.605
Everybody gets the pizza party gift card

00:01:59.605 --> 00:02:03.095
from Lou Malnati's to enjoy the Oscars.

00:02:03.095 --> 00:02:08.095
And I say have some slices
and watch some "Severance"

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:12.410
which is streaming now on Apple TV+,

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:14.940
and new episodes are
dropping every Friday.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.020
It's fantastic.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.010
I can't wait for everybody to see it.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.920
And Adam Scott, I'm so thrilled to finally

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.690
make your acquaintance
and my very best to you

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.860
and your whole family
including your Frankie.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.030
- Yes, and to your Frankie as well.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:29.863
Thank you.

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:32.870
I'm so thrilled to be on
your show and to meet you.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:33.851
Thanks so much.

00:02:33.851 --> 00:02:36.768
- [Drew] Oh, thank you, Adam Scott!

